    "description": "Send plain Discord messages from the unified `msg` envelope, with the title as the sender name and an optional profile picture.\n\nThe gateway posts directly to your Discord webhook: `body` becomes ordinary message content, `title` becomes the username, and an HTTPS `avatar_url` overrides the webhook avatar. The first image attachment appears in an image-only embed below the plain text. Links fold into the content. Long names and content are truncated to 80 and 2000 characters; reserved words in names are rewritten as dis_cord/cl_yde. Room metadata adds a protected six-character connector marker for backend echo refusal.\n\nCreate a webhook under Discord channel Settings → Integrations → Webhooks and save its full URL in DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL for the free gateway channel. Use gateway-plus for an additional destination selected by the enrollment's webhook_url_secret parameter. See How to use this service for examples and limits.",
